The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
free_transition_pgtable();
machine_kexec_cleanup();
```
Reason:
The bug occurs because both `init_transition_pgtable()` and `machine_kexec_cleanup()` (for 64-bit) or `machine_kexec_alloc_page_tables()` and `machine_kexec_cleanup()` (for 32-bit) call the page table free functions when memory allocation fails. This results in the same page table being freed multiple times, causing a double free error.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
image->arch.pgd = NULL;
image->arch.pmd0 = NULL;
image->arch.pte0 = NULL;
```
Reason:
The fix involves setting the pointers to NULL after freeing the page tables, which prevents subsequent calls to free the same page table again, thus avoiding the double free scenario. Centralizing the error handling ensures that the page tables are only freed once.

