The bug occurs because both `init_transition_pgtable()` and `machine_kexec_cleanup()` can call `free_transition_pgtable()` when memory allocation fails. If `init_transition_pgtable()` fails after allocating some pages, it calls `free_transition_pgtable()`, which frees the allocated pages. If `machine_kexec_cleanup()` is then called, it attempts to free the same pages again, leading to a double free error.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
