image->arch.pte = NULL;
```
Reason:
The fix involves removing the call to `free_transition_pgtable(image)` from the error handling in `init_transition_pgtable()`, thus preventing the double free scenario. Additionally, setting the pointers to `NULL` after freeing ensures that subsequent calls to free the same pages do not occur, as they will check for `NULL` before attempting to free. This centralizes error handling and avoids multiple frees of the same memory.

